    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. PHQ-2 0. AUDIT-C 2, below the risk threshold for men. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Pulmonary tuberculosis, treatment completed (A15.0)</content>. No symptoms of relapse two months after completing treatment. [S]<list><item>No routine tests; a skin or blood test would stay positive and is not repeated.</item><item>Same-day visit for a cough lasting more than two to three weeks, fever, night sweats, hemoptysis, or weight loss.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 1838-1839</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 1838-1839</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about three years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Immune by surface antibody at the tuberculosis diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence by his report</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative at the tuberculosis diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Antibody negative at the tuberculosis diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Tuberculosis testing</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated for active tuberculosis; the blood test stays positive; symptom review instead</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 2, below the risk threshold</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>112/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended from 35 for adults with overweight or obesity; BMI 19.4</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health and STI screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Discussed privately; no screening indicated by his history</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1838-1839 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Next preventive visit in one year; same-day visit for symptoms of relapse. [S]</paragraph></text>

